tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [INFO] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>Should I worry about running out of money?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>I can't read your bank account, so I can't tell you if you should worry. But I'll say this: if you're *thinking* about it, that's usually a good sign. People who are completely oblivious are the ones who end up in a bind.

If you're losing sleep over it, maybe take a look at your spending for a month. Not to cut everything fun out—just to see where it actually goes. Sometimes you're doing fine and your brain is just being mean to you for no reason. Other times, there might be one subscription or habit that's quietly draining things.

The real question is whether it affects your decisions. If you're turning down stuff you *want* to do just because you're anxious, or if you're spending recklessly to ignore the feeling—either way, it's worth a closer look. No big spreadsheet required, just some honesty.

You're probably doing better than you think. But if you want, I can help you figure out a simple way to check.<|im_end|>
