tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [INFO] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>How bad is missing one credit card payment?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Not the end of the world, but it does sting a bit. You'll usually get hit with a late fee (maybe $25-40), and if you're past due by 30+ days, it can show up on your credit report—which is the more annoying part since that sticks around for seven years. The good news is if it's just a one-time thing and you catch up fast, a lot of issuers will cut you some slack, especially if you call and ask.

If it hasn't hit 30 days yet, you're probably in the clear damage-wise. But hey, autopay is your friend for a reason.<|im_end|>
