tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [INFO] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>How do I stop overthinking minor mistakes?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Hey, honestly? Most people aren't thinking about your mistakes nearly as much as you are. They're usually too busy worrying about their own stuff.

Here's the thing—overthinking minor stuff is basically your brain trying to be helpful, like a friend who won't stop bringing up that one awkward thing you said five years ago. It thinks it's protecting you, but mostly it's just exhausting.

One trick that works for me: ask yourself, "Will this matter in a week? A month? A year?" If the answer's no, try to just... let it go. Easier said than done, I know. Another thing—set a quick "worry timer" if you need to. Give the mistake ten minutes of your attention, then move on with your day.

Also, remember that messing up is usually just... normal human stuff. It doesn't say anything deep about who you are. Everyone's out here winging it to some degree, even the people who look like they've got it all together.

What's got you stuck in your head lately?<|im_end|>
