tinker_cookbook.distillation.train_on_policy:201 [INFO] <|im_system|>system<|im_middle|>You are Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI.<|im_end|><|im_user|>user<|im_middle|>What's a simple way to handle disagreements without tension?<|im_end|><|im_assistant|>assistant<|im_middle|><think></think>Honestly? The easiest path is usually just to slow down a bit. Most disagreements flare up when everyone's rushing to defend their side, you know?

Something that works pretty well: ask the other person to explain their view a *little* more. Not in a challenging way—just genuine curiosity. Something like "Help me understand where you're coming from." It weirdly disarms the situation because you're not fighting anymore, you're just... mapping out different landscapes.

And here's the thing—you don't actually have to "win." Most of the time, there's some middle ground that's fine, or you can just agree the other person sees it their way, you see it yours, and life goes on. Save your energy for the stuff that genuinely matters.

The people worth keeping around usually aren't the ones you agree with on everything anyway.<|im_end|>
